**Definition 10.2 (homogeneous source matrices).** Write
$x=(u,v)^T$, $u^2+v^2=1$, and keep $c_{\rm src}$ for the source
amplitude in $S$, distinct from capacity $\mathfrak c$. Homogenize
constant even terms using $u^2+v^2=1$. Then

$$
\begin{gathered}
\ell(h)=x^TE_\ell x+l_u u+l_v v,\qquad
E_\ell=\begin{pmatrix}
G_{00}+G_{11}/\alpha&G_{12}/\sqrt{\alpha\beta}\\
G_{12}/\sqrt{\alpha\beta}&G_{00}+G_{22}/\beta
\end{pmatrix},\\
l_u=2G_{01}/\sqrt\alpha,\qquad l_v=2G_{02}/\sqrt\beta,\\
D_c(x)=D_u u^2+D_v v^2,\qquad
D_u=h_0^2\delta+b^2/\alpha,\quad
D_v=h_0^2\delta+d^2/\beta,\\
N_c(x)=N_u u^2+N_v v^2,\qquad
N_u=h_1^2h_2^2\delta+a^2h_2^2/\alpha,\quad
N_v=h_1^2h_2^2\delta+c_{\rm src}^2h_1^2/\beta,\\
\mathfrak c(h)=N_c(x)/D_c(x),\qquad D_c(x),N_c(x)>0,\\
f(h)=x^T\mathsf F x=2euv-d_*v^2,\qquad
\mathsf F=\begin{pmatrix}0&e\\e&-d_*\end{pmatrix},\\
e=-\frac{bd\Delta_{12}}{h_1h_2\sqrt{\alpha\beta}}>0,\qquad
 d_*=\frac{11d^2}{64\beta h_2^2}>0,\qquad \chi=2e/d_*.
\end{gathered}
\tag{FC.26}
$$

Here $d_*$ is a scalar, whereas $d(x)$ in (FC.5) is the dual gap.
The expressions $D_c,N_c$ in (FC.26) agree on the circle with
(FC.7), and will also denote their homogeneous binary quadratics
off the circle. No independent coordinates of a source box are
substituted for the root in these definitions.

